We are very bad at executing people. Depending on how you count, something like 7% of lethal injections in the US have been botched. This seemed very strange to me, so I dove into the numbers, looked at veterinary euthanasia, end-of-life care, and execution procedures, and what I found was that, almost certainly, the difference here is that a very high percentage of competent individuals refuse to engage in government executions.

I understand that, to many, killing a killer is a way of honoring life. I think that this has always been an ugly lie, but the fact that we cannot do it at all competently indicates to me that, as a society, we no longer actually believe it. 

Sources:
37 states haven't executed anyone in the last 5 years: https://deathpenaltyinfo.org/executions/executions-overview/states-with-no-recent-executions

23 states have abolished the death penalty: https://deathpenaltyinfo.org/executions/executions-overview/states-with-no-recent-executions

In 1847, Michigan became the first English-speaking government to abolish capital punishment (except for treason) https://www.michbar.org/programs/milestone/milestones_firsttoabolish

Tennessee Governor Bill Lee has suspended executions: https://www.reuters.com/world/us/tennessee-governor-calls-failed-christa-pike-execution-tragedy-2026-10-01/

Attempted execution of Krista Pike: https://www.reuters.com/world/us/tennessee-due-execute-woman-first-time-two-centuries-2026-09-30/

More background on pike: https://www.reuters.com/world/us/tennessee-governor-calls-failed-christa-pike-execution-tragedy-2026-10-01/

People sentenced to death have subsequently been exonerated: https://deathpenaltyinfo.org/facts-and-research/data/innocence

Joe Arridy was posthumously pardoned in 201: https://files.deathpenaltyinfo.org/legacy/ArridyPardon.pdf

Lethal injection is the most common execution method in the US: https://deathpenaltyinfo.org/executions/methods-of-execution

Info on Tennessee's protocols: https://apnews.com/article/225a47554413611c4626702c32a2577d

On IV Failure modes: https://www.nhsfife.org/services/all-services/patient-advice/infiltration-and-extravasation/

